content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, on the raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 3.2 mm/s. Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings; 3.2 mm/s lies between the 2.8 and 4.5 mm/s RMS boundaries, in Zone B, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS, restricted/plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, damage likely/stop the pump). The report does not state RMS or measurement location, so confirm both before final classification; the manual requires weekly measurements on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature is 68 C. The applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, and trip at 90 C; therefore 68 C is within the documented normal range and below both alarm and trip limits. Bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage is approximately one drop every two seconds (about 30 drops/min). No numerical allowable leakage limit is provided, but the troubleshooting table identifies leakage at the shaft seal as a symptom requiring seal replacement and an alignment check; treat the observed drip as a defect rather than accepting it as normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: premature failure of an installed HF3-450 component seal associated with the revised sleeve tolerance documented for HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000. P-108 is serial HF3-23110 and is in the affected range; confirm the installed seal and actual failure mode during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces are a documented probable cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have been run dry, which is another documented probable cause of leakage; no dry-running event is reported, so this remains unconfirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a documented possible cause of seal leakage. The current vibration and temperature readings do not exceed their documented restricted/high limits, but alignment still requires checking as part of the seal-leakage corrective action.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, verify and record vibration velocity as mm/s RMS on both bearing housings, identify the drive-end and non-drive-end values, and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Retain the existing 3.2 mm/s result as Zone B only if its RMS basis and housing measurement location are confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Arrange a controlled maintenance outage for the active shaft-seal leak. Continued running is not supported as a repair: the documented corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement plus an alignment check. Do not allow the pump to run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump, then remove the back pull-out assembly. The rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. When reassembling, tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm using the Table 5 condition of lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the existing seal and sleeve. Identify the installed seal, inspect the seal faces for wear or cracking, investigate any evidence of dry running, and inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure sleeve scoring depth and replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The bulletin only mandates replacement above that threshold; record the measured depth and condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit new cartridge mechanical seal HF3-450B; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. This does not eliminate the separate inspection for sleeve scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened, and reinstall the assembly using a new gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the HF3-450B M10 seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, superseding the manual's 25 Nm value for this application. Tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm where disturbed; Table 5 torques are for lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to a parallel offset tolerance of 0.05 mm and angular tolerance of 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Record the as-found and as-left alignment values.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge before operation and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Return the pump to service and verify that the shaft-seal drip has stopped. Recheck bearing-housing temperatures and vibration on both housings; apply the applicable limits of normal temperature up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, trip at 90 C, and the Figure 3 vibration zones. Escalate for bearing or impeller inspection and NPSH checks only if high vibration is subsequently confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; required replacement for HF3-450 on this pump because serial HF3-23110 is within the SB-2026-014 affected range. Gland nut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional replacement part. Have one available subject to site supply practice, but install only if inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry; its seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Confirm flush arrangements before returning it to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit seal HF3-450 to this affected pump. Use HF3-450B and apply its 30 Nm gland-nut torque rather than the superseded 25 Nm setting.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "An immediate vibration- or temperature-based stop is not indicated by the reported values: 3.2 mm/s is in Zone B if measured as specified, and 68 C is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. A stop would be required at vibration Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS) under Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: plan 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: plan 1.5 hours with 1 technician if alignment is performed as required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing; confirm whether disassembly/reassembly moves either before fixing the total outage duration.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not include the standard 6.0-hour, 2-technician bearing-replacement allowance as confirmed work: the reported temperature and vibration are within their documented normal/long-term-operation ranges, and bearing wear has not been established. The manual requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair if either shows wear, noise, or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: manual parts list C05 specifies component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 prohibits HF3-450 and requires cartridge HF3-450B on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000. P-108 is HF3-23110, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B is selected. The bulletin states that pumps below HF3-22000 remain on HF3-450 and manual Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual Table 5 lists 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because this asset is in the bulletin's serial range and will use HF3-450B, apply 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-setting conflict: manual procedure 5.2 includes withdrawing and inspecting the sleeve and general seal replacement, while SB-2026-014 says HF3-450B is pre-set and no sleeve measurement is needed. Treat this as no sleeve measurement for setting the pre-set cartridge; retain the bulletin's separate requirement to inspect scoring and replace the sleeve when depth exceeds 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 3.2 mm/s vibration an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and which housing produced it? What are the current readings on both bearing housings? These details are required for definitive Figure 3 classification (C06, C07).",
    "What is the actual seal leakage rate or acceptance criterion after repair? The evidence supplies the observed drip rate but no numerical allowable seal-leakage limit (C09).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, what is the observed failure mode, and is there any operating history of dry running or loss of Plan 11 flush? These facts are not in the report (C02, C09, C13).",
    "Does the pump's build or service history establish that SB-2026-014 has not already been embodied? The bulletin gives its issue date and serial applicability, but no build date or prior seal-replacement history is provided (C13).",
    "What is the measured shaft-sleeve scoring depth, and will HF3-455 require replacement? Replacement is mandatory only when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth (C13).",
    "Will the seal-replacement work move the motor or bearing housing and therefore require laser alignment under procedure 5.4? The final labour total depends on this (C10, C12).",
    "The evidence gives no priority classification, required completion date, operational consequence of the raw-water transfer pump being unavailable, isolation/LOTO procedure, or site permit requirements; these must be set by site operations and safety procedures.",
    "No post-repair maximum acceptable drip rate, flushing recommissioning steps, or detailed restart checks are documented beyond the Plan 11 flush and prohibition on dry running; obtain site or manufacturer guidance if numerical acceptance criteria are required (C02, C10)."
  ]
}
